Below are the key columns that will be useful for producing the requested breakdown, together with the most likely way each will be used and any typical filter / join conditions.

• DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS  
  • "Id": primary‑key for each death record – used to join to ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS."DeathRecordId".  
  • "Age": exact age of decedent – filter 12 ≤ Age ≤ 18.  
  • "AgeType": units of age (years, months, etc.).  (If needed, keep only records where "AgeType" = 1 → years.)  
  • "Race": numeric race code – join to RACE."Code" to see the textual description.  

• DEATH.DEATH.RACE  
  • "Code": numeric race code – join to DEATHRECORDS."Race".  
  • "Description": race name – look for ILIKE '%black%' to flag “Black” decedents.  

• DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS  
  • "DeathRecordId": links to DEATHRECORDS."Id".  
  • "Icd10Code": ICD‑10 code present anywhere on the entity axis list for that death.  

• DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE  
  • "Code": actual ICD‑10 code – join to ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS."Icd10Code".  
  • "Description": clinical text – use ILIKE '%vehicle%' or ILIKE '%firearm%' to classify causes.  

Typical conditions / joins that will appear in the queries  
• dr."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18  
• ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'   or   ic."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%'  
• r."Description" ILIKE '%black%'  
• dr."Id" = eac."DeathRecordId"  
• eac."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"  
• dr."Race" = r."Code"  

------------------------------------------------
Exploratory → progressively more complex SQL examples  
(Each query returns ≤ 20 rows, all identifiers are double‑quoted.)

```sql
-- 1) Sample death records for ages 12‑18 (no joins yet)
SELECT
    dr."Id",
    dr."Age",
    dr."AgeType",
    dr."Race"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
WHERE dr."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) List race codes whose description mentions “black”
SELECT
    r."Code",
    r."Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.RACE r
WHERE r."Description" ILIKE '%black%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) ICD‑10 codes whose description contains the word “vehicle”
SELECT
    ic."Code",
    ic."Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
WHERE ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) ICD‑10 codes whose description contains the word “firearm”
SELECT
    ic."Code",
    ic."Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
WHERE ic."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Entity‑axis rows (death‑to‑ICD10 linkage) involving a “vehicle” ICD‑10 description
SELECT
    eac."DeathRecordId",
    eac."Icd10Code"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS eac
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
      ON eac."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Ages 12‑18 with at least one “vehicle” ICD‑10 code (sample rows)
SELECT
    dr."Id",
    dr."Age",
    dr."Race",
    ic."Code"      AS "Icd10Code",
    ic."Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS eac
      ON dr."Id" = eac."DeathRecordId"
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
      ON eac."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE dr."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
  AND ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Ages 12‑18 with at least one “firearm” ICD‑10 code (sample rows)
SELECT
    dr."Id",
    dr."Age",
    dr."Race",
    ic."Code"      AS "Icd10Code",
    ic."Description"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS eac
      ON dr."Id" = eac."DeathRecordId"
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
      ON eac."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE dr."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
  AND ic."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Total number of vehicle‑related deaths per age (12‑18)
SELECT
    dr."Age",
    COUNT(DISTINCT dr."Id") AS "Death_Count_Vehicle"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS eac
      ON dr."Id" = eac."DeathRecordId"
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
      ON eac."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
WHERE dr."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
  AND ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
GROUP BY dr."Age"
ORDER BY dr."Age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Number of vehicle‑related deaths among “Black” decedents per age (12‑18)
SELECT
    dr."Age",
    COUNT(DISTINCT dr."Id") AS "Black_Death_Count_Vehicle"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS eac
      ON dr."Id" = eac."DeathRecordId"
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
      ON eac."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.RACE r
      ON dr."Race" = r."Code"
WHERE dr."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
  AND ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'
  AND r."Description" ILIKE '%black%'
GROUP BY dr."Age"
ORDER BY dr."Age"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Combined per‑age counts: total vs. Black for both “vehicle” and “firearm” deaths
SELECT
    dr."Age",
    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'  THEN dr."Id" END) AS "Vehicle_Total",
    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN ic."Description" ILIKE '%vehicle%'  AND r."Description" ILIKE '%black%' THEN dr."Id" END) AS "Vehicle_Black",
    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN ic."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%'  THEN dr."Id" END) AS "Firearm_Total",
    COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN ic."Description" ILIKE '%firearm%'  AND r."Description" ILIKE '%black%' THEN dr."Id" END) AS "Firearm_Black"
FROM DEATH.DEATH.DEATHRECORDS dr
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ENTITYAXISCONDITIONS eac
      ON dr."Id" = eac."DeathRecordId"
JOIN DEATH.DEATH.ICD10CODE ic
      ON eac."Icd10Code" = ic."Code"
LEFT JOIN DEATH.DEATH.RACE r
      ON dr."Race" = r."Code"
WHERE dr."Age" BETWEEN 12 AND 18
GROUP BY dr."Age"
ORDER BY dr."Age"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progress from simple column inspection to increasingly complex joins and aggregations, culminating in the single query (#10) that delivers the precise counts required for the analysis.
